From 3192116ad5c99ccd7f6edd59ad5e13cdd17d934d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sai Maddali <saimadda@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Apr 2026 16:30:04 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] QSDK:PROTOCOL:HOSTAPD: Fix use-after-free crash in scan timeout

A segfault can occur in wpa_driver_nl80211_scan_timeout() when accessing
BSS state after the BSS structure has already been freed.

The timeout is registered using a BSS context, but driver context can be
updated by first-BSS switching. A context mismatch can make the original
eloop_cancel_timeout() miss a pending scan timeout, leaving it to fire on
stale BSS state.

Fix this by using ELOOP_ALL_CTX in wpa_driver_nl80211_deinit() to cancel
all scan timeouts for the driver, regardless of the context used during
registration.

Backported from QSDK commit 3192116ad
("QSDK:PROTOCOL:HOSTAPD: Fix use-after-free crash in
wpa_driver_nl80211_scan_timeout").

Patch-dependency: None

Signed-off-by: sai Maddali <saimadda@qti.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Sidharth Renukadevi <srenukad@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
@@ -3428,7 +3428,7 @@ static void wpa_driver_nl80211_deinit(st
 	eloop_cancel_timeout(wpa_driver_nl80211_send_rfkill, drv, drv->ctx);
 	rfkill_deinit(drv->rfkill);
 
-	eloop_cancel_timeout(wpa_driver_nl80211_scan_timeout, drv, bss->ctx);
+	eloop_cancel_timeout(wpa_driver_nl80211_scan_timeout, drv, ELOOP_ALL_CTX);
 
 	if (!drv->start_iface_up)
 		(void) i802_set_iface_flags(bss, 0);
